{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.ParityViolationSkein","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.ParityViolationSkein","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cp_conservation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cp_conservation","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L95-L104","doc":"CP is conserved: the q ↔ q⁻¹ involution IS a symmetry.\nUnder CP: coeff_plus ↔ coeff_minus AND L₊ ↔ L₋,\nThe Skein relation maps to itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength_classical","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L88-L93","doc":"The parity violation strength vanishes at q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength_pos","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L80-L86","doc":"The parity violation strength is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parityViolationStrength","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L76-L78","doc":"At q = 1.1097, the parity violation parameter q - q⁻¹ ≈ 0.209. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L60-L74","doc":"The Skein relation is parity-invariant if and only if q = 1. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:parity-violation-skein","label":"prop:parity-violation-skein","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.parityInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.parityInvariant","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L55-L58","doc":"Parity invariance means the coefficients are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.coeff_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.coeff_minus","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Coefficient of [L₋]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.coeff_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.coeff_plus","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Coefficient of [L₊]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The parameter is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.q","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The deformation parameter (archimedean evaluation `q₀ ∈ ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinCoefficients","kind":"structure","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.lean#L41-L53","doc":"The Skein relation coefficients for L₊ and L₋.\nParity exchanges these: (q, q⁻¹) ↔ (q⁻¹, q).\nThe relation is parity-invariant iff q = q⁻¹, i.e., q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}